window.SAYINGS=[{"text":"And he said, \"Whoever finds the interpretation of these sayings will not experience death.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 1","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"Let him who seeks continue seeking until he finds. When he finds, he will become troubled. When he becomes troubled, he will be astonished, and he will rule over the All.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 2","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"If those who lead you say to you, 'See, the kingdom is in the sky,' then the birds of the sky will precede you. If they say to you, 'It is in the sea,' then the fish will precede you. Rather, the kingdom is inside of you, and it is outside of you. When you come to know yourselves, then you will become known, and you will realize that it is you who are the sons of the living father. But if you will not know yourselves, you dwell in poverty and it is you who are that poverty.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 3","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"The man old in days will not hesitate to ask a small child seven days old about the place of life, and he will live. For many who are first will become last, and they will become one and the same.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 4","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"Recognize what is in your sight, and that which is hidden from you will become plain to you . For there is nothing hidden which will not become manifest.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 5","source":"thomas"},{"text":"His disciples questioned him and said to him, \"Do you want us to fast? How shall we pray? Shall we give alms? What diet shall we observe?\" Jesus said, \"Do not tell lies, and do not do what you hate, for all things are plain in the sight of heaven. For nothing hidden will not become manifest, and nothing covered will remain without being uncovered.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 6","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"Blessed is the lion which becomes man when consumed by man; and cursed is the man whom the lion consumes, and the lion becomes man.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 7","source":"thomas"},{"text":"And he said, \"The man is like a wise fisherman who cast his net into the sea and drew it up from the sea full of small fish. Among them the wise fisherman found a fine large fish. He threw all the small fish back into the sea and chose the large fish without difficulty. Whoever has ears to hear, let him hear.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 8","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"Now the sower went out, took a handful (of seeds), and scattered them. Some fell on the road; the birds came and gathered them up. Others fell on the rock, did not take root in the soil, and did not produce ears. And others fell on thorns; they choked the seed(s) and worms ate them. And others fell on the good soil and it produced good fruit: it bore sixty per measure and a hundred and twenty per measure.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 9","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"I have cast fire upon the world, and see, I am guarding it until it blazes.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 10","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"This heaven will pass away, and the one above it will pass away. The dead are not alive, and the living will not die. In the days when you consumed what is dead, you made it what is alive. When you come to dwell in the light, what will you do? On the day when you were one you became two. But when you become two, what will you do?\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 11","source":"thomas"},{"text":"The disciples said to Jesus, \"We know that you will depart from us. Who is to be our leader?\" Jesus said to them, \"Wherever you are, you are to go to James the righteous, for whose sake heaven and earth came into being.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 12","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said to his disciples, \"Compare me to someone and tell me whom I am like.\" Simon Peter said to him, \"You are like a righteous angel.\" Matthew said to him, \"You are like a wise philosopher.\" Thomas said to him, \"Master, my mouth is wholly incapable of saying whom you are like.\" Jesus said, \"I am not your master. Because you have drunk, you have become intoxicated from the bubbling spring which I have measured out.\" And he took him and withdrew and told him three things. When Thomas returned to his companions, they asked him, \"What did Jesus say to you?\" Thomas said to them, \"If I tell you one of the things which he told me, you will pick up stones and throw them at me; a fire will come out of the stones and burn you up.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 13","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said to them, \"If you fast, you will give rise to sin for yourselves; and if you pray, you will be condemned; and if you give alms, you will do harm to your spirits. When you go into any land and walk about in the districts, if they receive you, eat what they will set before you, and heal the sick among them. For what goes into your mouth will not defile you, but that which issues from your mouth - it is that which will defile you.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 14","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"When you see one who was not born of woman, prostrate yourselves on your faces and worship him. That one is your father.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 15","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"Men think, perhaps, that it is peace which I have come to cast upon the world. They do not know that it is dissension which I have come to cast upon the earth: fire, sword, and war. For there will be five in a house: three will be against two, and two against three, the father against the son, and the son against the father. And they will stand solitary.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 16","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"I shall give you what no eye has seen and what no ear has heard and what no hand has touched and what has never occurred to the human mind.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 17","source":"thomas"},{"text":"The disciples said to Jesus, \"Tell us how our end will be.\" Jesus said, \"Have you discovered, then, the beginning, that you look for the end? For where the beginning is, there will the end be. Blessed is he who will take his place in the beginning; he will know the end and will not experience death.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 18","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"Blessed is he who came into being before he came into being. If you become my disciples and listen to my words, these stones will minister to you. For there are five trees for you in Paradise which remain undisturbed summer and winter and whose leaves do not fall. Whoever becomes acquainted with them will not experience death.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 19","source":"thomas"},{"text":"The disciples said to Jesus, \"Tell us what the kingdom of heaven is like.\" He said to them, \"It is like a mustard seed. It is the smallest of all seeds. But when it falls on tilled soil, it produces a great plant and becomes a shelter for birds of the sky.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 20","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Mary said to Jesus, \"Whom are your disciples like?\" He said, \"They are like children who have settled in a field which is not theirs. When the owners of the field come, they will say, 'Let us have back our field.' They (will) undress in their presence in order to let them have back their field and to give it back to them. Therefore I say, if the owner of a house knows that the thief is coming, he will begin his vigil before he comes and will not let him dig through into his house of his domain to carry away his goods. You, then, be on your guard against the world. Arm yourselves with great strength lest the robbers find a way to come to you, for the difficulty which you expect will (surely) materialize. Let there be among you a man of understanding. When the grain ripened, he came quickly with his sickle in his hand and reaped it. Whoever has ears to hear, let him hear.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 21","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus saw infants being suckled. He said to his disciples, \"These infants being suckled are like those who enter the kingdom.\" They said to him, \"Shall we then, as children, enter the kingdom?\" Jesus said to them, \"When you make the two one, and when you make the inside like the outside and the outside like the inside, and the above like the below, and when you make the male and the female one and the same, so that the male not be male nor the female female; and when you fashion eyes in the place of an eye, and a hand in place of a hand, and a foot in place of a foot, and a likeness in place of a likeness; then will you enter the kingdom.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 22","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"I shall choose you, one out of a thousand, and two out of ten thousand, and they shall stand as a single one.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 23","source":"thomas"},{"text":"His disciples said to him, \"Show us the place where you are, since it is necessary for us to seek it.\" He said to them, \"Whoever has ears, let him hear. There is light within a man of light, and he lights up the whole world. If he does not shine, he is darkness.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 24","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"Love your brother like your soul, guard him like the pupil of your eye.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 25","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"You see the mote in your brother's eye, but you do not see the beam in your own eye. When you cast the beam out of your own eye, then you will see clearly to cast the mote from your brother's eye.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 26","source":"thomas"},{"text":"<Jesus said,> \"If you do not fast as regards the world, you will not find the kingdom. If you do not observe the Sabbath as a Sabbath, you will not see the father.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 27","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"I took my place in the midst of the world, and I appeared to them in flesh. I found all of them intoxicated; I found none of them thirsty. And my soul became afflicted for the sons of men, because they are blind in their hearts and do not have sight; for empty they came into the world, and empty too they seek to leave the world. But for the moment they are intoxicated. When they shake off their wine, then they will repent.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 28","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"If the flesh came into being because of spirit, it is a wonder. But if spirit came into being because of the body, it is a wonder of wonders. Indeed, I am amazed at how this great wealth has made its home in this poverty.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 29","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"Where there are three gods, they are gods. Where there are two or one, I am with him.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 30","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"No prophet is accepted in his own village; no physician heals those who know him.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 31","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"A city being built on a high mountain and fortified cannot fall, nor can it be hidden.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 32","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"Preach from your housetops that which you will hear in your ear. For no one lights a lamp and puts it under a bushel, nor does he put it in a hidden place, but rather he sets it on a lampstand so that everyone who enters and leaves will see its light.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 33","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"If a blind man leads a blind man, they will both fall into a pit.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 34","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"It is not possible for anyone to enter the house of a strong man and take it by force unless he binds his hands; then he will (be able to) ransack his house.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 35","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"Do not be concerned from morning until evening and from evening until morning about what you will wear.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 36","source":"thomas"},{"text":"His disciples said, \"When will you become revealed to us and when shall we see you?\" Jesus said, \"When you disrobe without being ashamed and take up your garments and place them under your feet like little children and tread on them, then will you see the son of the living one, and you will not be afraid","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 37","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"Many times have you desired to hear these words which I am saying to you, and you have no one else to hear them from. There will be days when you will look for me and will not find me.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 38","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"The pharisees and the scribes have taken the keys of knowledge (gnosis) and hidden them. They themselves have not entered, nor have they allowed to enter those who wish to. You, however, be as wise as serpents and as innocent as doves.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 39","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"A grapevine has been planted outside of the father, but being unsound, it will be pulled up by its roots and destroyed.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 40","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"Whoever has something in his hand will receive more, and whoever has nothing will be deprived of even the little he has.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 41","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"Become passers-by.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 42","source":"thomas"},{"text":"His disciples said to him, \"Who are you, that you should say these things to us?\" <Jesus said to them,> \"You do not realize who I am from what I say to you, but you have become like the Jews, for they (either) love the tree and hate its fruit (or) love the fruit and hate the tree.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 43","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"Whoever blasphemes against the father will be forgiven, and whoever blasphemes against the son will be forgiven, but whoever blasphemes against the holy spirit will not be forgiven either on earth or in heaven.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 44","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"Grapes are not harvested from thorns, nor are figs gathered from thistles, for they do not produce fruit. A good man brings forth good from his storehouse; an evil man brings forth evil things from his evil storehouse, which is in his heart, and says evil things. For out of the abundance of the heart he brings forth evil things.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 45","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"Among those born of women, from Adam until John the Baptist, there is no one so superior to John the Baptist that his eyes should not be lowered (before him). Yet I have said, whichever one of you comes to be a child will be acquainted with the kingdom and will become superior to John.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 46","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"It is impossible for a man to mount two horses or to stretch two bows. And it is impossible for a servant to serve two masters; otherwise, he will honor the one and treat the other contemptuously. No man drinks old wine and immediately desires to drink new wine. And new wine is not put into old wineskins, lest they burst; nor is old wine put into a new wineskin, lest it spoil it. An old patch is not sewn onto a new garment, because a tear would result.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 47","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"If two make peace with each other in this one house, they will say to the mountain, 'Move Away,' and it will move away.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 48","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"Blessed are the solitary and elect, for you will find the kingdom. For you are from it, and to it you will return.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 49","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"If they say to you, 'Where did you come from?', say to them, 'We came from the light, the place where the light came into being on its own accord and established itself and became manifest through their image.' If they say to you, 'Is it you?', say, 'We are its children, we are the elect of the living father.' If they ask you, 'What is the sign of your father in you?', say to them, 'It is movement and repose.'\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 50","source":"thomas"},{"text":"His disciples said to him, \"When will the repose of the dead come about, and when will the new world come?\" He said to them, \"What you look forward to has already come, but you do not recognize it.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 51","source":"thomas"},{"text":"His disciples said to him, \"Twenty-four prophets spoke in Israel, and all of them spoke in you.\" He said to them, \"You have omitted the one living in your presence and have spoken (only) of the dead.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 52","source":"thomas"},{"text":"His disciples said to him, \"Is circumcision beneficial or not?\" He said to them, \"If it were beneficial, their father would beget them already circumcised from their mother. Rather, the true circumcision in spirit has become completely profitable.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 53","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"Blessed are the poor, for yours is the kingdom of heaven.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 54","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"Whoever does not hate his father and his mother cannot become a disciple to me. And whoever does not hate his brothers and sisters and take up his cross in my way will not be worthy of me.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 55","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"Whoever has come to understand the world has found (only) a corpse, and whoever has found a corpse is superior to the world.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 56","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"The kingdom of the father is like a man who had good seed. His enemy came by night and sowed weeds among the good seed. The man did not allow them to pull up the weeds; he said to them, 'I am afraid that you will go intending to pull up the weeds and pull up the wheat along with them.' For on the day of the harvest the weeds will be plainly visible, and they will be pulled up and burned.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 57","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"Blessed is the man who has suffered and found life.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 58","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"Take heed of the living one while you are alive, lest you die and seek to see him and be unable to do so.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 59","source":"thomas"},{"text":"<They saw> a Samaritan carrying a lamb on his way to Judea. He said to his disciples, \"That man is round about the lamb.\" They said to him, \"So that he may kill it and eat it.\" He said to them, \"While it is alive, he will not eat it, but only when he has killed it and it has become a corpse.\" They said to him, \"He cannot do so otherwise.\" He said to them, \"You too, look for a place for yourself within repose, lest you become a corpse and be eaten.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 60","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"Two will rest on a bed: the one will die, and the other will live.\" Salome said, \"Who are you, man, that you ... have come up on my couch and eaten from my table?\" Jesus said to her, \"I am he who exists from the undivided. I was given some of the things of my father.\" <...> \"I am your disciple.\" <...> \"Therefore I say, if he is destroyed, he will be filled with light, but if he is divided, he will be filled with darkness.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 61","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"It is to those who are worthy of my mysteries that I tell my mysteries. Do not let your left (hand) know what your right (hand) is doing.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 62","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"There was a rich man who had much money. He said, 'I shall put my money to use so that I may sow, reap, plant, and fill my storehouse with produce, with the result that I shall lack nothing.' Such were his intentions, but that same night he died. Let him who has ears hear.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 63","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"A man had received visitors. And when he had prepared the dinner, he sent his servant to invite the guests. He went to the first one and said to him, 'My master invites you.' He said, 'I have claims against some merchants. They are coming to me this evening. I must go and give them my orders. I ask to be excused from the dinner.' He went to another and said to him, 'My master has invited you.' He said to him, 'I have just bought a house and am required for the day. I shall not have any spare time.' He went to another and said to him, 'My master invites you.' He said to him, 'My friend is going to get married, and I am to prepare the banquet. I shall not be able to come. I ask to be excused from the dinner.' He went to another and said to him, 'My master invites you.' He said to him, 'I have just bought a farm, and I am on my way to collect the rent. I shall not be able to come. I ask to be excused.' The servant returned and said to his master, 'Those whom you invited to the dinner have asked to be excused.' The master said to his servant, 'Go outside to the streets and bring back those whom you happen to meet, so that they may dine.' Businessmen and merchants will not enter the places of my father.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 64","source":"thomas"},{"text":"He said, \"There was a good man who owned a vineyard. He leased it to tenant farmers so that they might work it and he might collect the produce from them. He sent his servant so that the tenants might give him the produce of the vineyard. They seized his servant and beat him, all but killing him. The servant went back and told his master. The master said, 'Perhaps he did not recognize them.' He sent another servant. The tenants beat this one as well. Then the owner sent his son and said, 'Perhaps they will show respect to my son.' Because the tenants knew that it was he who was the heir to the vineyard, they seized him and killed him. Let him who has ears hear.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 65","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"Show me the stone which the builders have rejected. That one is the cornerstone.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 66","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"If one who knows the all still feels a personal deficiency, he is completely deficient.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 67","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"Blessed are you when you are hated and persecuted. Wherever you have been persecuted they will find no place.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 68","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"Blessed are they who have been persecuted within themselves. It is they who have truly come to know the father. Blessed are the hungry, for the belly of him who desires will be filled.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 69","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"That which you have will save you if you bring it forth from yourselves. That which you do not have within you will kill you if you do not have it within you.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 70","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"I shall destroy this house, and no one will be able to build it [...].\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 71","source":"thomas"},{"text":"A man said to him, \"Tell my brothers to divide my father's possessions with me.\" He said to him, \"O man, who has made me a divider?\" He turned to his disciples and said to them, \"I am not a divider, am I?\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 72","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"The harvest is great but the laborers are few. Beseech the Lord, therefore, to send out laborers to the harvest.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 73","source":"thomas"},{"text":"He said, \"O Lord, there are many around the drinking trough, but there is nothing in the cistern.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 74","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"Many are standing at the door, but it is the solitary who will enter the bridal chamber.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 75","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"The kingdom of the father is like a merchant who had a consignment of merchandise and who discovered a pearl. That merchant was shrewd. He sold the merchandise and bought the pearl alone for himself. You too, seek his unfailing and enduring treasure where no moth comes near to devour and no worm destroys.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 76","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"It is I who am the light which is above them all. It is I who am the all. From me did the all come forth, and unto me did the all extend. Split a piece of wood, and I am there. Lift up the stone, and you will find me there.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 77","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"Why have you come out into the desert? To see a reed shaken by the wind? And to see a man clothed in fine garments like your kings and your great men? Upon them are the fine garments, and they are unable to discern the truth.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 78","source":"thomas"},{"text":"A woman from the crowd said to him, \"Blessed are the womb which bore you and the breasts which nourished you.\" He said to her, \"Blessed are those who have heard the word of the father and have truly kept it. For there will be days when you will say, 'Blessed are the womb which has not conceived and the breasts which have not given milk.'\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 79","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"He who has recognized the world has found the body, but he who has found the body is superior to the world.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 80","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"Let him who has grown rich be king, and let him who possesses power renounce it.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 81","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"He who is near me is near the fire, and he who is far from me is far from the kingdom.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 82","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"The images are manifest to man, but the light in them remains concealed in the image of the light of the father. He will become manifest, but his image will remain concealed by his light.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 83","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"When you see your likeness, you rejoice. But when you see your images which came into being before you, and which neither die not become manifest, how much you will have to bear!\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 84","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"Adam came into being from a great power and a great wealth, but he did not become worthy of you. For had he been worthy, he would not have experienced death.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 85","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"The foxes have their holes and the birds have their nests, but the son of man has no place to lay his head and rest.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 86","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"Wretched is the body that is dependant upon a body, and wretched is the soul that is dependent on these two.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 87","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"The angels and the prophets will come to you and give to you those things you (already) have. And you too, give them those things which you have, and say to yourselves, 'When will they come and take what is theirs?'\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 88","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"Why do you wash the outside of the cup? Do you not realize that he who made the inside is the same one who made the outside?\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 89","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"Come unto me, for my yoke is easy and my lordship is mild, and you will find repose for yourselves.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 90","source":"thomas"},{"text":"They said to him, \"Tell us who you are so that we may believe in you.\" He said to them, \"You read the face of the sky and of the earth, but you have not recognized the one who is before you, and you do not know how to read this moment.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 91","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"Seek and you will find. Yet, what you asked me about in former times and which I did not tell you then, now I do desire to tell, but you do not inquire after it.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 92","source":"thomas"},{"text":"<Jesus said,> \"Do not give what is holy to dogs, lest they throw them on the dung-heap. Do not throw the pearls to swine, lest they [...] it [...].\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 93","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"He who seeks will find, and he who knocks will be let in.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 94","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"If you have money, do not lend it at interest, but give it to one from whom you will not get it back.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 95","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"The kingdom of the father is like a certain woman. She took a little leaven, concealed it in some dough, and made it into large loaves. Let him who has ears hear.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 96","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"The kingdom of the father is like a certain woman who was carrying a jar full of meal. While she was walking on the road, still some distance from home, the handle of the jar broke and the meal emptied out behind her on the road. She did not realize it; she had noticed no accident. When she reached her house, she set the jar down and found it empty.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 97","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"The kingdom of the father is like a certain man who wanted to kill a powerful man. In his own house he drew his sword and stuck it into the wall in order to find out whether his hand could carry through. Then he slew the powerful man.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 98","source":"thomas"},{"text":"The disciples said to him, \"Your brothers and your mother are standing outside.\" He said to them, \"Those here who do the will of my father are my brothers and my mother. It is they who will enter the kingdom of my father.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 99","source":"thomas"},{"text":"They showed Jesus a gold coin and said to him, \"Caesar's men demand taxes from us.\" He said to them, \"Give Caesar what belongs to Caesar, give God what belongs to God, and give me what is mine.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 100","source":"thomas"},{"text":"<Jesus said,> \"Whoever does not hate his father and his mother as I do cannot become a disciple to me. And whoever does not love his father and his mother as I do cannot become a disciple to me. For my mother [...], but my true mother gave me life.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 101","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"Woe to the pharisees, for they are like a dog sleeping in the manger of oxen, for neither does he eat nor does he let the oxen eat.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 102","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"Fortunate is the man who knows where the brigands will enter, so that he may get up, muster his domain, and arm himself before they invade.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 103","source":"thomas"},{"text":"They said to Jesus, \"Come, let us pray today and let us fast.\" Jesus said, \"What is the sin that I have committed, or wherein have I been defeated? But when the bridegroom leaves the bridal chamber, then let them fast and pray.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 104","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"He who knows the father and the mother will be called the son of a harlot.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 105","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"When you make the two one, you will become the sons of man, and when you say, 'Mountain, move away,' it will move away.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 106","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"The kingdom is like a shepherd who had a hundred sheep. One of them, the largest, went astray. He left the ninety-nine sheep and looked for that one until he found it. When he had gone to such trouble, he said to the sheep, 'I care for you more than the ninety-nine.'\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 107","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"He who will drink from my mouth will become like me. I myself shall become he, and the things that are hidden will be revealed to him.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 108","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"The kingdom is like a man who had a hidden treasure in his field without knowing it. And after he died, he left it to his son. The son did not know (about the treasure). He inherited the field and sold it. And the one who bought it went plowing and found the treasure. He began to lend money at interest to whomever he wished.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 109","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"Whoever finds the world and becomes rich, let him renounce the world.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 110","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"The heavens and the earth will be rolled up in your presence. And the one who lives from the living one will not see death.\" Does not Jesus say, \"Whoever finds himself is superior to the world?\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 111","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Jesus said, \"Woe to the flesh that depends on the soul; woe to the soul that depends on the flesh.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 112","source":"thomas"},{"text":"His disciples said to him, \"When will the kingdom come?\" <Jesus said,> \"It will not come by waiting for it. It will not be a matter of saying 'here it is' or 'there it is.' Rather, the kingdom of the father is spread out upon the earth, and men do not see it.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 113","source":"thomas"},{"text":"Simon Peter said to him, \"Let Mary leave us, for women are not worthy of life.\" Jesus said, \"I myself shall lead her in order to make her male, so that she too may become a living spirit resembling you males. For every woman who will make herself male will enter the kingdom of heaven.\"","citation":"Gospel of Thomas · Saying 114","source":"thomas"},{"text":"The Lord said to the disciples, \"[...] from every house. Bring into the house of the Father. But do not take (anything) in the house of the Father nor carry it off.\"","citation":"Gospel of Philip · Philip ¶13","source":"philip"},{"text":"He said, \"He who shall not eat my flesh and drink my blood has not life in him\" (Jn 6:53).","citation":"Gospel of Philip · Philip ¶17","source":"philip"},{"text":"He said on that day in the thanksgiving, \"You who have joined the perfect light with the Holy Spirit, unite the angels with us also, as being the images.\"","citation":"Gospel of Philip · Philip ¶20","source":"philip"},{"text":"A disciple asked the Lord one day for something of this world. He said to him, \"Ask your mother, and she will give you of the things which are another's.\"","citation":"Gospel of Philip · Philip ¶24","source":"philip"},{"text":"The Lord went into the dye works of Levi. He took seventy-two different colors and threw them into the vat. He took them out all white. And he said, \"Even so has the Son of Man come as a dyer.\"","citation":"Gospel of Philip · Philip ¶41","source":"philip"},{"text":"The Savior answered and said to them, \"Why do I not love you like her?\"","citation":"Gospel of Philip · Philip ¶42","source":"philip"},{"text":"When a blind man and one who sees are both together in darkness, they are no different from one another. When the light comes, then he who sees will see the light, and he who is blind will remain in darkness.","citation":"Gospel of Philip · Philip ¶42","source":"philip"},{"text":"The Lord said, \"Blessed is he who is before he came into being. For he who is, has been and shall be.\"","citation":"Gospel of Philip · Philip ¶43","source":"philip"},{"text":"He said, \"I came to make the things below like the things above, and the things outside like those inside. I came to unite them in the place.\"","citation":"Gospel of Philip · Philip ¶54","source":"philip"},{"text":"He said, \"My Father who is in secret\".","citation":"Gospel of Philip · Philip ¶55","source":"philip"},{"text":"He said, \"Go into your chamber and shut the door behind you, and pray to your Father who is in secret\" (Mt 6:6).","citation":"Gospel of Philip · Philip ¶55","source":"philip"},{"text":"\"My God, my God, why, O Lord, have you forsaken me?\" (Mk 15:34). It was on the cross that he said these words, for he had departed from that place.","citation":"Gospel of Philip · Philip ¶58","source":"philip"},{"text":"For he said, \"Thus we should fulfill all righteousness.\" (Mt 3:15)","citation":"Gospel of Philip · Philip ¶73","source":"philip"},{"text":"The Lord said it well: \"Some have entered the Kingdom of Heaven laughing, and they have come out [...]\".","citation":"Gospel of Philip · Philip ¶79","source":"philip"},{"text":"\"He who sins is the slave of sin\" (Jn 8:34).","citation":"Gospel of Philip · Philip ¶88","source":"philip"},{"text":"That is why the Word says, \"Already the axe is laid at the root of the trees\" (Mt 3:10).","citation":"Gospel of Philip · Philip ¶98","source":"philip"},{"text":"The Word said, \"If you know the truth, the truth will make you free\" (Jn 8:32).","citation":"Gospel of Philip · Philip ¶98","source":"philip"},{"text":"\"Every plant which my father who is in heaven has not planted will be plucked out.\" (Mt 15:13)","citation":"Gospel of Philip · Philip ¶100","source":"philip"},{"text":"The Lord would not have said \"My Father who is in Heaven\" (Mt 16:17).","citation":"Gospel of Philip · Philip ¶12","source":"philip"},{"text":"Already the time has come, brothers, for us to abandon our labor and stand at rest. For whoever stands at rest will rest forever.","citation":"Dialogue of the Saviour · Opening","source":"dialogue"},{"text":"But when I came, I opened the path, and I taught them about the passage which they will traverse.","citation":"Dialogue of the Saviour · The path","source":"dialogue"},{"text":"The lamp of the body is the mind. As long as the things inside you are set in order, your bodies are luminous.","citation":"Dialogue of the Saviour · The lamp of the body","source":"dialogue"},{"text":"It is the one who speaks who also listens, and it is the one who can see who also reveals.","citation":"Dialogue of the Saviour · To Matthew","source":"dialogue"},{"text":"There was darkness and water, and spirit upon water.","citation":"Dialogue of the Saviour · Before heaven and earth","source":"dialogue"},{"text":"If someone sets his soul up high, then he will be exalted.","citation":"Dialogue of the Saviour · The true mind","source":"dialogue"},{"text":"I say to you, let him who possesses power renounce it and repent.","citation":"Dialogue of the Saviour · To Matthew","source":"dialogue"},{"text":"Brother Matthew, you will not be able to see it as long as you are carrying flesh around.","citation":"Dialogue of the Saviour · The place of life","source":"dialogue"},{"text":"Everyone who has known himself has seen it in everything given to him to do.","citation":"Dialogue of the Saviour · To Matthew","source":"dialogue"},{"text":"That which supports the earth is that which supports the heaven.","citation":"Dialogue of the Saviour · The stone","source":"dialogue"},{"text":"For the earth does not move. Were it to move, it would fall.","citation":"Dialogue of the Saviour · The stone","source":"dialogue"},{"text":"If one does not stand in the darkness, he will not be able to see the light.","citation":"Dialogue of the Saviour · On the elements","source":"dialogue"},{"text":"And how will someone who does not know the Son know the Father?","citation":"Dialogue of the Saviour · On the elements","source":"dialogue"},{"text":"Whoever will not understand how he came will not understand how he will go.","citation":"Dialogue of the Saviour · On the elements","source":"dialogue"},{"text":"Have I not told you that like a visible voice and flash of lightning will the good be taken up to the light?","citation":"Dialogue of the Saviour · To his disciples","source":"dialogue"},{"text":"It is you who will rule over them! But when you rid yourselves of jealousy, then you will clothe yourselves in light and enter the bridal chamber.","citation":"Dialogue of the Saviour · The governors","source":"dialogue"},{"text":"You are from the fullness, and you dwell in the place where the deficiency is. And lo! His light has poured down upon me!","citation":"Dialogue of the Saviour · Fullness and deficiency","source":"dialogue"},{"text":"How do you wish to see it? By means of a transient vision or an eternal vision?","citation":"Dialogue of the Saviour · The great vision","source":"dialogue"},{"text":"Strive to save that which can follow you, and to seek it out, and to speak from within it, so that, as you seek it out, everything might be in harmony with you.","citation":"Dialogue of the Saviour · Strive to save","source":"dialogue"},{"text":"Whatever is born of truth does not die. Whatever is born of woman dies.","citation":"Dialogue of the Saviour · On dying and living","source":"dialogue"},{"text":"The place where I am not!","citation":"Dialogue of the Saviour · To Mary","source":"dialogue"},{"text":"When you lay down these burdens!","citation":"Dialogue of the Saviour · On rest","source":"dialogue"},{"text":"When you abandon the works which will not be able to follow you, then you will rest.","citation":"Dialogue of the Saviour · The small and the big","source":"dialogue"},{"text":"Love and goodness. For if one of these existed among the governors, wickedness would never have come into existence.","citation":"Dialogue of the Saviour · The beginning of the path","source":"dialogue"},{"text":"You have understood all the things I have said to you, and you have accepted them on faith. If you have known them, then they are yours. If not, then they are not yours.","citation":"Dialogue of the Saviour · The end of everything","source":"dialogue"},{"text":"Stand in the place you can reach!","citation":"Dialogue of the Saviour · The place to which we go","source":"dialogue"},{"text":"I have told you that it is the one who can see who reveals.","citation":"Dialogue of the Saviour · To Mary","source":"dialogue"},{"text":"Pray in the place where there is no woman.","citation":"Dialogue of the Saviour · On prayer","source":"dialogue"},{"text":"I am come forth out of that First Mystery, which is the last mystery, that is the four-and-twentieth mystery.","citation":"Pistis Sophia · First Book, ch. 1","source":"pistis"},{"text":"Who hath ears to hear, let him hear.","citation":"Pistis Sophia · First Book, ch. 17","source":"pistis"},{"text":"Mary, thou blessed one, whom I will perfect in all mysteries of those of the height, discourse in openness, thou, whose heart is raised to the kingdom of heaven more than all thy brethren.","citation":"Pistis Sophia · First Book, ch. 17","source":"pistis"},{"text":"Finely [said], Matthew. Now, therefore, amēn, I say unto you: When the perfect number is completed and the universe is raised hence, I will take my seat in the Treasury of the Light, and ye yourselves will sit on twelve light-powers, until we have restored all the orders of the twelve saviours to the region of the inheritances of every one of them.","citation":"Pistis Sophia · First Book, ch. 50","source":"pistis"},{"text":"Well said, finely. Amēn, amēn, I say unto thee: They shall proclaim thee blessed from one end of the earth to the other; for the pledge of the First Mystery hath taken up its abode with thee, and through that pledge shall all from the earth and all from the height be saved, and that pledge is the beginning and the end.","citation":"Pistis Sophia · First Book, ch. 59","source":"pistis"},{"text":"Question concerning what thou desirest to question, and I will reveal it unto thee with precision and certainty and without similitude.","citation":"Pistis Sophia · Second Book, ch. 88","source":"pistis"},{"text":"A day of the Light is a thousand years in the world, so that thirty-six-myriads of years and a half-myriad of years of the world are a single year of the Light.","citation":"Pistis Sophia · Second Book, ch. 99","source":"pistis"},{"text":"And ye, my disciples, and every one who shall receive the mystery of the Ineffable, will abide with me on my right and on my left, being kings with me in my kingdom.","citation":"Pistis Sophia · Second Book, ch. 99","source":"pistis"},{"text":"Question concerning that on which thou desirest to question, and I will reveal it unto thee face to face without similitude.","citation":"Pistis Sophia · Second Book, ch. 100","source":"pistis"},{"text":"How long am I to endure you? How long am I to bear with you? Have ye then not even yet understood and are ye ignorant?","citation":"Pistis Sophia · Second Book, ch. 100","source":"pistis"},{"text":"That ye all one with another are out of one and the same paste and the same matter and the same substance, and that ye all are out of the same Mixture.","citation":"Pistis Sophia · Second Book, ch. 100","source":"pistis"},{"text":"For this cause have I said unto you aforetime: 'Seek, that ye may find.'","citation":"Pistis Sophia · Second Book, ch. 100","source":"pistis"},{"text":"Amēn, I say unto you: For the sake of the race of men, because it is material, I have torn myself asunder and brought unto them all the mysteries of the Light, that I may purify them, for they are the refuse of the whole matter of their matter; else would no soul of the total race of men have been saved, and they would not be able to inherit the kingdom of the Light, if I had not brought unto them the purifying mysteries.","citation":"Pistis Sophia · Second Book, ch. 100","source":"pistis"},{"text":"The healthy have no need of the physician, but the sick.","citation":"Pistis Sophia · Second Book, ch. 100","source":"pistis"},{"text":"Cease not to seek day and night and remit not yourselves until ye find the purifying mysteries which will purify you and make you into a refined light, so that ye will go on high and inherit the light of my kingdom.","citation":"Pistis Sophia · Second Book, ch. 100","source":"pistis"},{"text":"Renounce the whole world and the whole matter therein, that ye may not amass other additional matter to the rest of your matter in you.","citation":"Pistis Sophia · Second Book, ch. 100","source":"pistis"},{"text":"I forgive and will forgive; for this cause, therefore, hath the First Mystery sent me, that I may forgive every one his sins.","citation":"Pistis Sophia · Second Book, ch. 100","source":"pistis"},{"text":"When I shall have gone into the Light, then herald it unto the whole world and say unto them: Cease not to seek day and night and remit not yourselves until ye find the mysteries of the Light-kingdom, which will purify you and make you into refined light and lead you into the Light-kingdom.","citation":"Pistis Sophia · Third Book, ch. 102","source":"pistis"},{"text":"Say unto them: Renounce the whole world and the whole matter therein and all its care and all its sins, in a word all its associations which are in it, that ye may be worthy of the mysteries of the Light and be saved from all the chastisements which are in the judgments.","citation":"Pistis Sophia · Third Book, ch. 102","source":"pistis"},{"text":"Say unto them: Be ye merciful, that ye may receive the mysteries of the Light and go on high into the Light-kingdom.","citation":"Pistis Sophia · Third Book, ch. 102","source":"pistis"},{"text":"Say unto them: Give ye alms, that ye may receive the mysteries of the Light and go on high into the Light-kingdom.","citation":"Pistis Sophia · Third Book, ch. 102","source":"pistis"},{"text":"Say unto them: Minister unto the poor and the sick and distressed, that ye may receive the mysteries of the Light and go on high into the Light-kingdom.","citation":"Pistis Sophia · Third Book, ch. 102","source":"pistis"},{"text":"Say unto them: Renounce all, that ye may receive the mysteries of the Light and go on high into the Light-kingdom.","citation":"Pistis Sophia · Third Book, ch. 102","source":"pistis"},{"text":"For it is because of sinfulness that I have brought the mysteries into the world, that I may forgive all their sins which they have committed from the beginning on.","citation":"Pistis Sophia · Third Book, ch. 102","source":"pistis"},{"text":"I am not come to call the righteous.","citation":"Pistis Sophia · Third Book, ch. 102","source":"pistis"},{"text":"For the mysteries are the gift of the First Mystery, that he may wipe out the sins and iniquities of all sinners.","citation":"Pistis Sophia · Third Book, ch. 102","source":"pistis"},{"text":"But amēn, amēn, I say unto you: Even if a righteous man hath committed no sins at all, he cannot possibly be brought into the Light-kingdom, because the sign of the kingdom of the mysteries is not with him. In a word, it is impossible to bring souls into the Light without the mysteries of the Light-kingdom.","citation":"Pistis Sophia · Third Book, ch. 103","source":"pistis"},{"text":"It is these alone which will receive the repentance of that man and forgive his sins; for those mysteries in sooth are compassionate and merciful-minded and forgiving at every time.","citation":"Pistis Sophia · Third Book, ch. 105","source":"pistis"},{"text":"Now, therefore, he who shall receive the mysteries of the baptisms, then the mystery of them becometh a great, exceedingly violent, wise fire and it burneth up the sins and entereth into the soul secretly and consumeth all the sins which the counterfeiting spirit hath made fast on to it.","citation":"Pistis Sophia · Third Book, ch. 115","source":"pistis"},{"text":"Amēn, I say unto thee: The fire in Amente is nine times fiercer than the fire in mankind.","citation":"Pistis Sophia · Fourth Book, ch. 127","source":"pistis"},{"text":"If they receive the mystery when still in life, and if they come out of the body, they become light-beams and light-streams and penetrate all the regions until they reach the region of their inheritance.","citation":"Pistis Sophia · Fourth Book, ch. 129","source":"pistis"},{"text":"Question what thou wilt.","citation":"Pistis Sophia · Fifth Book, ch. 139","source":"pistis"},{"text":"“Repent! For the Kingdom of Heaven is at hand.”","citation":"Matthew 4:17 · World English Bible","source":"matthew","meaning":"Jesus announces that God’s reign is near and calls for a changed heart and direction."},{"text":"“Blessed are the poor in spirit, for theirs is the Kingdom of Heaven. Blessed are those who mourn, for they shall be comforted. Blessed are the gentle, for they shall inherit the earth. Blessed are those who hunger and thirst after righteousness, for they shall be filled. Blessed are the merciful, for they shall obtain mercy. Blessed are the pure in heart, for they shall see God. Blessed are the peacemakers, for they shall be called children of God. Blessed are those who have been persecuted for righteousness’ sake, for theirs is the Kingdom of Heaven.”","citation":"Matthew 5:3–10 · World English Bible","source":"matthew","meaning":"The Beatitudes name God’s favor on people the world often overlooks and describe the character of life in God’s kingdom."},{"text":"“You are the salt of the earth, but if the salt has lost its flavor, with what will it be salted?”","citation":"Matthew 5:13 · World English Bible","source":"matthew","meaning":"Disciples are meant to preserve what is good and give life its moral and spiritual savor."},{"text":"“You are the light of the world. A city located on a hill can’t be hidden. Let your light shine before men, that they may see your good works and glorify your Father who is in heaven.”","citation":"Matthew 5:14–16 · World English Bible","source":"matthew","meaning":"Faith is meant to become visible through good works that direct attention toward God, not toward personal glory."},{"text":"“Don’t think that I came to destroy the law or the prophets. I didn’t come to destroy, but to fulfill.”","citation":"Matthew 5:17 · World English Bible","source":"matthew","meaning":"Jesus presents his teaching as bringing Scripture to its intended fullness rather than discarding it."},{"text":"“If therefore you are offering your gift at the altar, and there remember that your brother has anything against you, leave your gift there before the altar, and go your way. First be reconciled to your brother, and then come and offer your gift.”","citation":"Matthew 5:23–24 · World English Bible","source":"matthew","meaning":"Reconciliation with another person is treated as part of worship, not as something spirituality can bypass."},{"text":"“But let your ‘Yes’ be ‘Yes’ and your ‘No’ be ‘No.’ Whatever is more than these is of the evil one.”","citation":"Matthew 5:37 · World English Bible","source":"matthew","meaning":"Simple, dependable truthfulness should make elaborate oaths unnecessary."},{"text":"“Whoever strikes you on your right cheek, turn to him the other also. If anyone sues you to take away your coat, let him have your cloak also. Whoever compels you to go one mile, go with him two.”","citation":"Matthew 5:39–42 · World English Bible","source":"matthew","meaning":"Jesus teaches a courageous nonretaliation that refuses to let injury dictate one’s character."},{"text":"“Love your enemies, bless those who curse you, do good to those who hate you, and pray for those who mistreat you and persecute you, that you may be children of your Father who is in heaven.”","citation":"Matthew 5:44–45 · World English Bible","source":"matthew","meaning":"Divine love crosses the boundary between friend and enemy and seeks another’s good even under hostility."},{"text":"“When you do merciful deeds, don’t let your left hand know what your right hand does, so that your merciful deeds may be in secret; then your Father who sees in secret will reward you openly.”","citation":"Matthew 6:3–4 · World English Bible","source":"matthew","meaning":"Generosity is most faithful when it is freed from the need for applause."},{"text":"“Our Father in heaven, may your name be kept holy. Let your Kingdom come. Let your will be done on earth as it is in heaven. Give us today our daily bread. Forgive us our debts, as we also forgive our debtors. Bring us not into temptation, but deliver us from the evil one.”","citation":"Matthew 6:9–13 · World English Bible","source":"matthew","meaning":"The Lord’s Prayer gathers worship, trust, daily dependence, forgiveness, and moral protection into one pattern of prayer."},{"text":"“Don’t lay up treasures for yourselves on the earth, where moth and rust consume, and where thieves break through and steal; but lay up for yourselves treasures in heaven. For where your treasure is, there your heart will be also.”","citation":"Matthew 6:19–21 · World English Bible","source":"matthew","meaning":"What we treat as our true treasure gradually claims the loyalty and direction of the heart."},{"text":"“Don’t be anxious for your life, what you will eat or what you will drink; nor yet for your body, what you will wear. Isn’t life more than food, and the body more than clothing? Which of you by being anxious can add one moment to his lifespan?”","citation":"Matthew 6:25–27 · World English Bible","source":"matthew","meaning":"Jesus does not deny real needs; he challenges anxiety’s claim that worry can secure life."},{"text":"“Seek first God’s Kingdom and his righteousness; and all these things will be given to you as well. Therefore don’t be anxious for tomorrow, for tomorrow will be anxious for itself.”","citation":"Matthew 6:33–34 · World English Bible","source":"matthew","meaning":"Put God’s justice and reign first, and meet today faithfully instead of living inside tomorrow’s fears."},{"text":"“Don’t judge, so that you won’t be judged. For with whatever judgment you judge, you will be judged. First remove the beam out of your own eye, and then you can see clearly to remove the speck out of your brother’s eye.”","citation":"Matthew 7:1–5 · World English Bible","source":"matthew","meaning":"Moral discernment begins with honest self-examination rather than hypocritical condemnation."},{"text":"“Ask, and it will be given you. Seek, and you will find. Knock, and it will be opened for you. For everyone who asks receives. He who seeks finds. To him who knocks it will be opened.”","citation":"Matthew 7:7–8 · World English Bible","source":"matthew","meaning":"Prayer and spiritual searching are pictured as active, persistent trust rather than passive wishing."},{"text":"“Therefore, whatever you desire for men to do to you, you shall also do to them; for this is the law and the prophets.”","citation":"Matthew 7:12 · World English Bible","source":"matthew","meaning":"The Golden Rule turns empathy into action: give others the treatment you would hope to receive."},{"text":"“Enter in by the narrow gate; for wide is the gate and broad is the way that leads to destruction, and many are those who enter in by it. How narrow is the gate and restricted is the way that leads to life! Few are those who find it.”","citation":"Matthew 7:13–14 · World English Bible","source":"matthew","meaning":"The path to life requires deliberate commitment; popularity is not proof that a way is good."},{"text":"“Everyone therefore who hears these words of mine and does them, I will liken him to a wise man who built his house on a rock. The rain came down, the floods came, and the winds blew and beat on that house; and it didn’t fall, for it was founded on the rock.”","citation":"Matthew 7:24–25 · World English Bible","source":"matthew","meaning":"Hearing becomes wisdom only when it is practiced; lived teaching forms a foundation that can withstand crisis."},{"text":"“Come to me, all you who labor and are heavily burdened, and I will give you rest. Take my yoke upon you and learn from me, for I am gentle and humble in heart; and you will find rest for your souls. For my yoke is easy, and my burden is light.”","citation":"Matthew 11:28–30 · World English Bible","source":"matthew","meaning":"Jesus offers weary people a gentler way of life shaped by humility, learning, and shared burden."},{"text":"“Unless you turn and become as little children, you will in no way enter into the Kingdom of Heaven. Whoever therefore humbles himself as this little child is the greatest in the Kingdom of Heaven.”","citation":"Matthew 18:3–4 · World English Bible","source":"matthew","meaning":"Greatness in God’s kingdom begins in humility, dependence, and openness rather than status."},{"text":"“I don’t tell you until seven times, but, until seventy times seven.”","citation":"Matthew 18:21–22 · World English Bible","source":"matthew","meaning":"Forgiveness is not to be rationed by a small tally; it is meant to become a settled disposition."},{"text":"“Whoever desires to become great among you shall be your servant. Whoever desires to be first among you shall be your bondservant, even as the Son of Man came not to be served, but to serve, and to give his life as a ransom for many.”","citation":"Matthew 20:26–28 · World English Bible","source":"matthew","meaning":"Jesus overturns ordinary power: true greatness is measured by service and self-giving."},{"text":"“You shall love the Lord your God with all your heart, with all your soul, and with all your mind. This is the first and great commandment. A second likewise is this, ‘You shall love your neighbor as yourself.’ The whole law and the prophets depend on these two commandments.”","citation":"Matthew 22:37–40 · World English Bible","source":"matthew","meaning":"Love of God and love of neighbor are the center from which every other command must be understood."},{"text":"“All authority has been given to me in heaven and on earth. Go and make disciples of all nations, baptizing them in the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, teaching them to observe all things that I commanded you. Behold, I am with you always, even to the end of the age.”","citation":"Matthew 28:18–20 · World English Bible","source":"matthew","meaning":"The Great Commission joins worldwide witness, teaching, initiation, and the promise of Christ’s continuing presence."},{"text":"“The time is fulfilled, and God’s Kingdom is at hand! Repent, and believe in the Good News.”","citation":"Mark 1:15 · World English Bible","source":"mark","meaning":"Jesus begins his public message with urgency: God’s reign is near, so trust and direction must change."},{"text":"“Those who are healthy have no need for a physician, but those who are sick. I came not to call the righteous, but sinners to repentance.”","citation":"Mark 2:17 · World English Bible","source":"mark","meaning":"Jesus compares his mission to a doctor’s work: mercy moves toward those who know they need healing."},{"text":"“The Sabbath was made for man, not man for the Sabbath. Therefore the Son of Man is lord even of the Sabbath.”","citation":"Mark 2:27–28 · World English Bible","source":"mark","meaning":"Sacred practice is meant to serve human flourishing; rules are not masters that erase mercy."},{"text":"“Whoever does the will of God is my brother, my sister, and mother.”","citation":"Mark 3:35 · World English Bible","source":"mark","meaning":"Shared obedience to God creates a spiritual family that reaches beyond biological ties."},{"text":"“God’s Kingdom is as if a man should cast seed on the earth, and should sleep and rise night and day, and the seed should spring up and grow, though he doesn’t know how. But when the fruit is ripe, immediately he puts in the sickle, because the harvest has come.”","citation":"Mark 4:26–29 · World English Bible","source":"mark","meaning":"God’s work often grows quietly beyond our control; the disciple’s role is faithful planting and readiness for harvest."},{"text":"“How will we liken God’s Kingdom? It’s like a grain of mustard seed, which, when it is sown in the earth, though it is less than all the seeds that are on the earth, yet when it is sown, grows up and becomes greater than all the herbs.”","citation":"Mark 4:30–32 · World English Bible","source":"mark","meaning":"The kingdom can begin almost invisibly and still grow into sheltering, surprising abundance."},{"text":"“Peace! Be still! Why are you so afraid? How is it that you have no faith?”","citation":"Mark 4:39–40 · World English Bible","source":"mark","meaning":"The calming of the storm becomes a call to trust even when circumstances feel overwhelming."},{"text":"“There is nothing from outside of the man that going into him can defile him; but the things which proceed out of the man are those that defile the man.”","citation":"Mark 7:15 · World English Bible","source":"mark","meaning":"Moral impurity is rooted in what the heart produces, not merely in external contact or ritual categories."},{"text":"“Whoever wants to come after me, let him deny himself, and take up his cross, and follow me. For whoever wants to save his life will lose it; and whoever will lose his life for my sake and the Good News’ sake will save it. For what does it profit a man to gain the whole world and forfeit his life?”","citation":"Mark 8:34–36 · World English Bible","source":"mark","meaning":"Discipleship asks for costly self-surrender and measures gain by the life of the soul, not possession of the world."},{"text":"“If any man wants to be first, he shall be last of all and servant of all.”","citation":"Mark 9:35 · World English Bible","source":"mark","meaning":"In Jesus’ community, leadership is proved by taking the lowest place in service."},{"text":"“Whoever receives one such little child in my name receives me, and whoever receives me doesn’t receive me, but him who sent me.”","citation":"Mark 9:37 · World English Bible","source":"mark","meaning":"Welcoming someone with little status is treated as welcoming Christ and the One who sent him."},{"text":"“For whoever is not against us is on our side. For whoever will give you a cup of water to drink in my name because you are Christ’s, most certainly I tell you, he will in no way lose his reward.”","citation":"Mark 9:40–41 · World English Bible","source":"mark","meaning":"Jesus resists needless exclusion and honors even small acts of kindness done in good faith."},{"text":"“Have salt in yourselves, and be at peace with one another.”","citation":"Mark 9:50 · World English Bible","source":"mark","meaning":"Inner integrity and peace with others belong together."},{"text":"“Allow the little children to come to me! Don’t forbid them, for God’s Kingdom belongs to such as these. Most certainly I tell you, whoever will not receive God’s Kingdom like a little child, he will in no way enter into it.”","citation":"Mark 10:14–15 · World English Bible","source":"mark","meaning":"The kingdom is received with a child’s openness and dependence, not seized as an achievement."},{"text":"“With men it is impossible, but not with God, for all things are possible with God.”","citation":"Mark 10:27 · World English Bible","source":"mark","meaning":"Human limits do not define the reach of divine possibility."},{"text":"“Whoever wants to become great among you shall be your servant. Whoever of you wants to become first among you shall be bondservant of all. For the Son of Man also came not to be served but to serve, and to give his life as a ransom for many.”","citation":"Mark 10:43–45 · World English Bible","source":"mark","meaning":"Jesus defines authority through service and places his own self-giving at the center of that pattern."},{"text":"“Have faith in God. All things whatever you pray and ask for, believe that you have received them, and you shall have them. Whenever you stand praying, forgive, if you have anything against anyone.”","citation":"Mark 11:22–25 · World English Bible","source":"mark","meaning":"Trusting prayer cannot be separated from a forgiving heart."},{"text":"“The first of all the commandments is, ‘Hear, Israel, the Lord our God, the Lord is one: you shall love the Lord your God with all your heart, with all your soul, with all your mind, and with all your strength.’ The second is like this, ‘You shall love your neighbor as yourself.’ There is no other commandment greater than these.”","citation":"Mark 12:29–31 · World English Bible","source":"mark","meaning":"Whole-person love of God and practical love of neighbor form one inseparable center of faith."},{"text":"“Watch, keep alert, and pray; for you don’t know when the time is.”","citation":"Mark 13:33 · World English Bible","source":"mark","meaning":"Spiritual readiness means sustained attention and prayer rather than anxious date-setting."},{"text":"“Abba, Father, all things are possible to you. Please remove this cup from me. However, not what I desire, but what you desire.”","citation":"Mark 14:36 · World English Bible","source":"mark","meaning":"Jesus’ prayer holds honest anguish and willing trust together without pretending the suffering is easy."},{"text":"“The Spirit of the Lord is on me, because he has anointed me to preach good news to the poor. He has sent me to heal the broken hearted, to proclaim release to the captives, recovering of sight to the blind, to deliver those who are crushed, and to proclaim the acceptable year of the Lord.”","citation":"Luke 4:18–19 · World English Bible","source":"luke","meaning":"Jesus describes his mission as good news, healing, liberation, restored sight, and God’s favor for the vulnerable."},{"text":"“Blessed are you who are poor, for God’s Kingdom is yours. Blessed are you who hunger now, for you will be filled. Blessed are you who weep now, for you will laugh.”","citation":"Luke 6:20–21 · World English Bible","source":"luke","meaning":"Luke’s blessings announce a concrete reversal for people living with poverty, hunger, and grief."},{"text":"“Love your enemies, do good to those who hate you, bless those who curse you, and pray for those who mistreat you.”","citation":"Luke 6:27–28 · World English Bible","source":"luke","meaning":"Jesus calls love beyond reciprocity, toward active goodwill even for an enemy."},{"text":"“As you would like people to do to you, do exactly so to them.”","citation":"Luke 6:31 · World English Bible","source":"luke","meaning":"Empathy becomes an ethical rule when we actively offer the treatment we hope to receive."},{"text":"“Therefore be merciful, even as your Father is also merciful.”","citation":"Luke 6:36 · World English Bible","source":"luke","meaning":"Mercy is presented as an imitation of God’s own character."},{"text":"“Don’t judge, and you won’t be judged. Don’t condemn, and you won’t be condemned. Set free, and you will be set free. Give, and it will be given to you.”","citation":"Luke 6:37–38 · World English Bible","source":"luke","meaning":"The measure we extend through mercy, release, and generosity shapes the measure we receive."},{"text":"“Therefore I tell you, her sins, which are many, are forgiven, for she loved much. But one to whom little is forgiven, loves little.”","citation":"Luke 7:47 · World English Bible","source":"luke","meaning":"A deep experience of forgiveness can awaken deep gratitude and love."},{"text":"“My mother and my brothers are these who hear the word of God and do it.”","citation":"Luke 8:21 · World English Bible","source":"luke","meaning":"Spiritual kinship is formed by listening to God and putting that hearing into practice."},{"text":"“If anyone desires to come after me, let him deny himself, take up his cross, and follow me. For whoever desires to save his life will lose it, but whoever will lose his life for my sake will save it.”","citation":"Luke 9:23–24 · World English Bible","source":"luke","meaning":"Following Jesus means releasing self-preservation as the highest good and accepting the cost of faithful love."},{"text":"“Whoever receives this little child in my name receives me. Whoever receives me receives him who sent me. For whoever is least among you all, this one will be great.”","citation":"Luke 9:48 · World English Bible","source":"luke","meaning":"How we welcome the least powerful reveals how we welcome God; humility is true greatness."},{"text":"“The harvest is indeed plentiful, but the laborers are few. Pray therefore to the Lord of the harvest that he may send out laborers into his harvest.”","citation":"Luke 10:2 · World English Bible","source":"luke","meaning":"The need is abundant, and the first response is prayer for people willing to serve it."},{"text":"“You shall love the Lord your God with all your heart, with all your soul, with all your strength, and with all your mind; and your neighbor as yourself. You have answered correctly. Do this, and you will live.”","citation":"Luke 10:27–28 · World English Bible","source":"luke","meaning":"Love is not merely the right answer; it becomes life when practiced toward God and neighbor."},{"text":"“Now which of these three do you think seemed to be a neighbor to him who fell among the robbers? Go and do likewise.”","citation":"Luke 10:36–37 · World English Bible","source":"luke","meaning":"The Good Samaritan turns “neighbor” from a category into a merciful action toward the person in need."},{"text":"“Martha, Martha, you are anxious and troubled about many things, but one thing is needed. Mary has chosen the good part, which will not be taken away from her.”","citation":"Luke 10:41–42 · World English Bible","source":"luke","meaning":"Jesus invites anxious busyness to yield to attentive presence and what matters most."},{"text":"“On the contrary, blessed are those who hear the word of God, and keep it.”","citation":"Luke 11:28 · World English Bible","source":"luke","meaning":"Blessing rests not on proximity or admiration alone but on hearing that becomes faithful action."},{"text":"“Beware! Keep yourselves from covetousness, for a man’s life doesn’t consist of the abundance of the things which he possesses.”","citation":"Luke 12:15 · World English Bible","source":"luke","meaning":"A person’s life and worth cannot be measured by accumulated possessions."},{"text":"“Don’t be afraid, little flock, for it is your Father’s good pleasure to give you the Kingdom. Sell that which you have and give gifts to the needy. Make for yourselves purses which don’t grow old, a treasure in the heavens that doesn’t fail. For where your treasure is, there will your heart be also.”","citation":"Luke 12:32–34 · World English Bible","source":"luke","meaning":"Freedom from fear opens into generosity, and generosity reveals where the heart’s true security lies."},{"text":"“Therefore be ready also, for the Son of Man is coming in an hour that you don’t expect him.”","citation":"Luke 12:40 · World English Bible","source":"luke","meaning":"Readiness is a way of living faithfully now, not an excuse for prediction."},{"text":"“Strive to enter in by the narrow door, for many, I tell you, will seek to enter in and will not be able.”","citation":"Luke 13:24 · World English Bible","source":"luke","meaning":"Spiritual life calls for earnest commitment rather than vague interest."},{"text":"“For everyone who exalts himself will be humbled, and whoever humbles himself will be exalted.”","citation":"Luke 14:11 · World English Bible","source":"luke","meaning":"God’s kingdom reverses self-promotion and honors humility."},{"text":"“Which of you men, if you had one hundred sheep and lost one of them, wouldn’t leave the ninety-nine in the wilderness and go after the one that was lost until he found it? I tell you that even so there will be more joy in heaven over one sinner who repents than over ninety-nine righteous people who need no repentance.”","citation":"Luke 15:4–7 · World English Bible","source":"luke","meaning":"God’s seeking love values each lost person and celebrates restoration rather than resenting it."},{"text":"“He who is faithful in a very little is faithful also in much. He who is dishonest in a very little is also dishonest in much.”","citation":"Luke 16:10 · World English Bible","source":"luke","meaning":"Character is revealed in small responsibilities long before larger ones arrive."},{"text":"“If your brother sins against you, rebuke him. If he repents, forgive him. If he sins against you seven times in the day, and seven times returns, saying, ‘I repent,’ you shall forgive him.”","citation":"Luke 17:3–4 · World English Bible","source":"luke","meaning":"Forgiveness can be repeatedly renewed while still naming wrongdoing honestly."},{"text":"“God’s Kingdom doesn’t come with observation; neither will they say, ‘Look, here!’ or, ‘Look, there!’ for behold, God’s Kingdom is within you.”","citation":"Luke 17:20–21 · World English Bible","source":"luke","meaning":"The reign of God is not a spectacle to be located from a distance; it is already present among and within those who receive it."},{"text":"“Everyone who exalts himself will be humbled, but he who humbles himself will be exalted.”","citation":"Luke 18:14 · World English Bible","source":"luke","meaning":"The humble person who asks for mercy stands closer to God than the proud person who advertises virtue."},{"text":"“For the Son of Man came to seek and to save that which was lost.”","citation":"Luke 19:10 · World English Bible","source":"luke","meaning":"Jesus summarizes his mission as active rescue and restoration, not detached judgment."},{"text":"“He who is the greater among you, let him become as the younger, and he who is governing, as he who serves. I am among you as he who serves.”","citation":"Luke 22:26–27 · World English Bible","source":"luke","meaning":"Christian authority is modeled on Jesus’ own presence as a servant."},{"text":"“Father, forgive them, for they don’t know what they are doing.”","citation":"Luke 23:34 · World English Bible","source":"luke","meaning":"At the point of violence, Jesus answers with intercession and forgiveness rather than revenge."},{"text":"“Most certainly I tell you, unless one is born anew, he can’t see God’s Kingdom.”","citation":"John 3:3 · World English Bible","source":"john","meaning":"Life with God requires a beginning so deep that Jesus describes it as a new birth."},{"text":"“Unless one is born of water and Spirit, he can’t enter into God’s Kingdom. That which is born of the flesh is flesh. That which is born of the Spirit is spirit.”","citation":"John 3:5–6 · World English Bible","source":"john","meaning":"Jesus contrasts ordinary birth with the inward life created by God’s Spirit."},{"text":"“For God so loved the world, that he gave his only born Son, that whoever believes in him should not perish, but have eternal life. For God didn’t send his Son into the world to judge the world, but that the world should be saved through him.”","citation":"John 3:16–17 · World English Bible","source":"john","meaning":"The heart of Jesus’ mission is God’s self-giving love and the rescue of the world, not its condemnation."},{"text":"“Everyone who drinks of this water will thirst again, but whoever drinks of the water that I will give him will never thirst again; but the water that I will give him will become in him a well of water springing up to eternal life.”","citation":"John 4:13–14 · World English Bible","source":"john","meaning":"Living water symbolizes divine life received inwardly as an enduring source rather than a temporary satisfaction."},{"text":"“The true worshipers will worship the Father in spirit and truth, for the Father seeks such to be his worshipers. God is spirit, and those who worship him must worship in spirit and truth.”","citation":"John 4:23–24 · World English Bible","source":"john","meaning":"True worship is not confined to a location; it joins inward reality with truthfulness before God."},{"text":"“He who hears my word and believes him who sent me has eternal life, and doesn’t come into judgment, but has passed out of death into life.”","citation":"John 5:24 · World English Bible","source":"john","meaning":"Trust in Jesus and the One who sent him is described as a present passage from death into life."},{"text":"“You search the Scriptures, because you think that in them you have eternal life; and these are they which testify about me. Yet you will not come to me, that you may have life.”","citation":"John 5:39–40 · World English Bible","source":"john","meaning":"Scripture can point toward life while still being used to avoid the living encounter to which it testifies."},{"text":"“I am the bread of life. Whoever comes to me will not be hungry, and whoever believes in me will never be thirsty.”","citation":"John 6:35 · World English Bible","source":"john","meaning":"Jesus presents himself as the enduring nourishment for the deepest human hunger and thirst."},{"text":"“I am the living bread which came down out of heaven. If anyone eats of this bread, he will live forever.”","citation":"John 6:51 · World English Bible","source":"john","meaning":"The image of living bread expresses a life from God that must be received and made part of oneself."},{"text":"“If anyone is thirsty, let him come to me and drink! He who believes in me, as the Scripture has said, from within him will flow rivers of living water.”","citation":"John 7:37–38 · World English Bible","source":"john","meaning":"Divine life does not only satisfy the receiver; it becomes a source of life flowing outward to others."},{"text":"“I am the light of the world. He who follows me will not walk in the darkness, but will have the light of life.”","citation":"John 8:12 · World English Bible","source":"john","meaning":"Following Jesus is pictured as leaving confusion and death for an illuminating way of life."},{"text":"“If you remain in my word, then you are truly my disciples. You will know the truth, and the truth will make you free.”","citation":"John 8:31–32 · World English Bible","source":"john","meaning":"Freedom grows from continuing in Jesus’ teaching until truth becomes lived knowledge."},{"text":"“Everyone who commits sin is the bondservant of sin. If therefore the Son makes you free, you will be free indeed.”","citation":"John 8:34–36 · World English Bible","source":"john","meaning":"Wrongdoing can become a form of slavery; Jesus promises a freedom deeper than outward circumstance."},{"text":"“Most certainly, I tell you, before Abraham came into existence, I AM.”","citation":"John 8:58 · World English Bible","source":"john","meaning":"Jesus speaks of an identity that precedes Abraham and evokes the divine name revealed in Scripture."},{"text":"“While I am in the world, I am the light of the world.”","citation":"John 9:5 · World English Bible","source":"john","meaning":"Jesus identifies his presence with light that reveals, guides, and gives life."},{"text":"“I am the door. If anyone enters in by me, he will be saved, and will go in and go out, and will find pasture. I came that they may have life, and may have it abundantly.”","citation":"John 10:9–10 · World English Bible","source":"john","meaning":"The door and pasture images present Jesus as the way into safety, freedom, nourishment, and abundant life."},{"text":"“I am the good shepherd. The good shepherd lays down his life for the sheep.”","citation":"John 10:11 · World English Bible","source":"john","meaning":"Jesus defines good leadership by protective, self-giving love rather than control."},{"text":"“My sheep hear my voice, and I know them, and they follow me. I give eternal life to them. They will never perish, and no one will snatch them out of my hand.”","citation":"John 10:27–28 · World English Bible","source":"john","meaning":"The shepherd image joins recognition, relationship, guidance, and enduring security."},{"text":"“I am the resurrection and the life. He who believes in me will still live, even if he dies. Whoever lives and believes in me will never die. Do you believe this?”","citation":"John 11:25–26 · World English Bible","source":"john","meaning":"Resurrection is centered in Jesus himself and offered as a hope stronger than physical death."},{"text":"“Unless a grain of wheat falls into the earth and dies, it remains by itself alone. But if it dies, it bears much fruit. If anyone serves me, let him follow me. Where I am, there will my servant also be.”","citation":"John 12:24–26 · World English Bible","source":"john","meaning":"The seed pictures self-giving death as the path to fruitfulness and frames discipleship as following Jesus through it."},{"text":"“I have come as a light into the world, that whoever believes in me may not remain in the darkness. If anyone listens to my sayings and doesn’t believe, I don’t judge him. For I came not to judge the world, but to save the world.”","citation":"John 12:46–47 · World English Bible","source":"john","meaning":"Jesus describes his purpose as illumination and rescue rather than condemnation."},{"text":"“If I then, the Lord and the Teacher, have washed your feet, you also ought to wash one another’s feet. For I have given you an example, that you also should do as I have done to you.”","citation":"John 13:14–15 · World English Bible","source":"john","meaning":"No status is too high for humble service; Jesus’ action becomes the pattern for his followers."},{"text":"“A new commandment I give to you, that you love one another. Just as I have loved you, you also love one another. By this everyone will know that you are my disciples, if you have love for one another.”","citation":"John 13:34–35 · World English Bible","source":"john","meaning":"The recognizable mark of discipleship is love shaped by Jesus’ own self-giving example."},{"text":"“Don’t let your heart be troubled. Believe in God. Believe also in me. In my Father’s house are many homes. I am going to prepare a place for you. I will come again and will receive you to myself; that where I am, you may be there also.”","citation":"John 14:1–3 · World English Bible","source":"john","meaning":"Jesus offers troubled disciples trust, belonging, and the promise of restored presence."},{"text":"“I am the way, the truth, and the life. No one comes to the Father except through me.”","citation":"John 14:6 · World English Bible","source":"john","meaning":"Jesus presents himself not merely as a teacher of the path but as the path, truth, and life that lead to the Father."},{"text":"“If you love me, keep my commandments. I will pray to the Father, and he will give you another Counselor, that he may be with you forever: the Spirit of truth.”","citation":"John 14:15–17 · World English Bible","source":"john","meaning":"Love becomes obedience, and Jesus promises the abiding help and presence of the Spirit of truth."},{"text":"“Peace I leave with you. My peace I give to you; not as the world gives, I give to you. Don’t let your heart be troubled, neither let it be fearful.”","citation":"John 14:27 · World English Bible","source":"john","meaning":"Jesus gives a peace not dependent on favorable conditions and speaks it directly into fear."},{"text":"“I am the true vine, and my Father is the farmer. Remain in me, and I in you. As the branch can’t bear fruit by itself unless it remains in the vine, so neither can you, unless you remain in me. Apart from me you can do nothing.”","citation":"John 15:1–5 · World English Bible","source":"john","meaning":"The vine pictures spiritual fruit as the result of an ongoing, living union with Christ."},{"text":"“Even as the Father has loved me, I also have loved you. Remain in my love. If you keep my commandments, you will remain in my love.”","citation":"John 15:9–10 · World English Bible","source":"john","meaning":"Jesus invites disciples to dwell in the same current of love that joins him to the Father."},{"text":"“This is my commandment, that you love one another, even as I have loved you. Greater love has no one than this, that someone lay down his life for his friends.”","citation":"John 15:12–13 · World English Bible","source":"john","meaning":"Love reaches its fullest expression in freely giving oneself for another’s good."},{"text":"“If the world hates you, you know that it has hated me before it hated you. A servant is not greater than his lord. If they persecuted me, they will also persecute you.”","citation":"John 15:18–20 · World English Bible","source":"john","meaning":"Disciples should not mistake opposition for proof of failure; faithfulness may share in Jesus’ rejection."},{"text":"“When he, the Spirit of truth, has come, he will guide you into all truth.”","citation":"John 16:13 · World English Bible","source":"john","meaning":"Jesus promises that the Spirit will continue guiding the community into truth."},{"text":"“In the world you have trouble; but cheer up! I have overcome the world.”","citation":"John 16:33 · World English Bible","source":"john","meaning":"Jesus combines realism about suffering with courage grounded in his victory over the world’s power."},{"text":"“May they all be one, even as you, Father, are in me, and I in you, that they also may be one in us. … I in them, and you in me, that they may be perfected into one.”","citation":"John 17:21, 23 · World English Bible","source":"john","meaning":"Jesus prays for a unity among his followers that reflects divine communion and becomes a witness to love."},{"text":"“My Kingdom is not of this world. If my Kingdom were of this world, then my servants would fight.”","citation":"John 18:36 · World English Bible","source":"john","meaning":"Jesus distinguishes his kingdom from political power maintained through violence."},{"text":"“It is finished.”","citation":"John 19:30 · World English Bible","source":"john","meaning":"Jesus’ final declaration from the cross presents his mission as brought to completion."},{"text":"“Because you have seen me, you have believed. Blessed are those who have not seen, and have believed.”","citation":"John 20:29 · World English Bible","source":"john","meaning":"Jesus blesses the trust of later disciples who respond without Thomas’s direct sight."},{"text":"“Don’t depart from Jerusalem, but wait for the promise of the Father, which you heard from me. For John indeed baptized in water, but you will be baptized in the Holy Spirit not many days from now.”","citation":"Acts 1:4–5 · World English Bible","source":"acts","meaning":"The risen Jesus asks the disciples to wait for divine empowerment rather than beginning their mission in their own strength."},{"text":"“It isn’t for you to know times or seasons which the Father has set within his own authority. But you will receive power when the Holy Spirit has come upon you. You will be witnesses to me in Jerusalem, in all Judea and Samaria, and to the uttermost parts of the earth.”","citation":"Acts 1:7–8 · World English Bible","source":"acts","meaning":"Jesus redirects speculation about dates toward Spirit-empowered witness across every boundary."},{"text":"“Saul, Saul, why do you persecute me? I am Jesus, whom you are persecuting. But rise up and enter into the city, and you will be told what you must do.”","citation":"Acts 9:4–6 · World English Bible","source":"acts","meaning":"Jesus identifies himself with the people Saul harms and turns a persecutor toward a new calling."},{"text":"“Don’t be afraid, but speak and don’t be silent; for I am with you, and no one will attack you to harm you, for I have many people in this city.”","citation":"Acts 18:9–10 · World English Bible","source":"acts","meaning":"The Lord answers Paul’s fear with presence, protection, and the assurance that he is not alone."},{"text":"“It is more blessed to give than to receive.”","citation":"Acts 20:35 · World English Bible","source":"acts","meaning":"This saying remembered by Paul condenses Jesus’ way of life into generous self-giving."},{"text":"“Cheer up, Paul, for as you have testified about me at Jerusalem, so you must testify also at Rome.”","citation":"Acts 23:11 · World English Bible","source":"acts","meaning":"In danger and confinement, Jesus gives Paul courage and a purpose that reaches beyond the present crisis."},{"text":"“Saul, Saul, why are you persecuting me? It is hard for you to kick against the goads. I am Jesus, whom you are persecuting. Arise and stand on your feet, for I have appeared to you for this purpose: to appoint you a servant and a witness, to open their eyes, that they may turn from darkness to light and from the power of Satan to God.”","citation":"Acts 26:14–18 · World English Bible","source":"acts","meaning":"Jesus transforms Saul’s resistance into a mission of witness, awakening, and liberation."},{"text":"“This is my body, which is for you. Do this in memory of me. This cup is the new covenant in my blood. Do this, as often as you drink, in memory of me.”","citation":"1 Corinthians 11:24–25 · World English Bible","source":"letters","meaning":"At the shared meal, Jesus gives his followers a repeated act of remembrance centered on his self-giving and the new covenant."},{"text":"“My grace is sufficient for you, for my power is made perfect in weakness.”","citation":"2 Corinthians 12:9 · World English Bible","source":"letters","meaning":"Christ’s grace does not always remove weakness; it can reveal divine strength within it."},{"text":"“Don’t be afraid. I am the first and the last, and the Living one. I was dead, and behold, I am alive forever and ever. Amen. I have the keys of Death and of Hades.”","citation":"Revelation 1:17–18 · World English Bible","source":"revelation","meaning":"The risen Jesus answers fear with his victory over death and his enduring authority."},{"text":"“I have this against you, that you left your first love. Remember therefore from where you have fallen, and repent and do the first works.”","citation":"Revelation 2:4–5 · World English Bible","source":"revelation","meaning":"Religious endurance is not enough without love; renewal begins by remembering, turning, and acting again from that love."},{"text":"“Don’t be afraid of the things which you are about to suffer. Be faithful to death, and I will give you the crown of life.”","citation":"Revelation 2:10 · World English Bible","source":"revelation","meaning":"Jesus calls for courageous faithfulness under suffering and promises life beyond what persecution can take."},{"text":"“He who has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the assemblies. To him who overcomes, to him I will give of the hidden manna, and I will give him a white stone, and on the stone a new name written which no one knows but he who receives it.”","citation":"Revelation 2:17 · World English Bible","source":"revelation","meaning":"Hidden manna and a new name picture intimate nourishment, vindication, and identity given by God."},{"text":"“He who overcomes will be arrayed in white garments, and I will in no way blot his name out of the book of life, and I will confess his name before my Father and before his angels.”","citation":"Revelation 3:5 · World English Bible","source":"revelation","meaning":"Jesus promises cleansing, secure belonging, and public acknowledgment to those who remain faithful."},{"text":"“I am coming quickly! Hold firmly that which you have, so that no one takes your crown. He who overcomes, I will make him a pillar in the temple of my God, and he will go out from there no more.”","citation":"Revelation 3:11–12 · World English Bible","source":"revelation","meaning":"Perseverance leads to an image of lasting stability, belonging, and nearness to God."},{"text":"“As many as I love, I reprove and chasten. Be zealous therefore, and repent. Behold, I stand at the door and knock. If anyone hears my voice and opens the door, then I will come in to him and will dine with him, and he with me.”","citation":"Revelation 3:19–20 · World English Bible","source":"revelation","meaning":"Correction is framed by love, and repentance opens into the intimacy of a shared meal with Christ."},{"text":"“Behold, I come quickly. Blessed is he who keeps the words of the prophecy of this book.”","citation":"Revelation 22:7 · World English Bible","source":"revelation","meaning":"Hope for Christ’s coming is joined to faithful attention in the present."},{"text":"“Behold, I come quickly. My reward is with me, to repay to each man according to his work. I am the Alpha and the Omega, the First and the Last, the Beginning and the End.”","citation":"Revelation 22:12–13 · World English Bible","source":"revelation","meaning":"Jesus speaks as the Lord of history who brings justice and encompasses creation’s beginning and completion."},{"text":"“I, Jesus, have sent my angel to testify these things to you for the assemblies. I am the root and the offspring of David, the Bright and Morning Star.”","citation":"Revelation 22:16 · World English Bible","source":"revelation","meaning":"Jesus identifies himself as both David’s source and heir, and as the light announcing a new day."},{"text":"“Yes, I come quickly.”","citation":"Revelation 22:20 · World English Bible","source":"revelation","meaning":"The Bible closes Jesus’ direct speech with a promise of return that calls forth hope and readiness."}];
